Faxbot: polled transmission for HylaFAX+ 7.0.11 (T.30 role reversal), so the
SSL Fax engine can be polled (applies after 0001-sslfax-address-policy.patch).

What changes:

- faxd/polldoc.h (new): the held-document rules. A document a caller may
  collect is a TIFF in pollq with a sidecar of the same name and the suffix
  ".poll" (number=, selective=, password=, job=, tsi=, tagline=, held=).
  Which document a DTC gets, and why one is refused, is decided here; the
  image build compiles and runs tests/polled_transmit_test.c++ against it.
- faxd/FaxRecv.c++, FaxServer.h/.c++: before faxgetty sends its DIS it reads
  the sidecars held for the caller's number (Caller ID). With one, the DIS
  says "ready to transmit" (T.30 Table 2, bit 9). A caller that answers with
  (PWD) (SEP) (CIG) DTC gets the oldest document its SEP and PWD name through
  the ordinary send path (sendClientCapabilitiesOK, sendFaxPhaseB,
  Class1Modem::sendPhaseB, sendEnd), the DTC standing in for the DIS; any
  other DTC is refused with DCN (T.30 5.3.6.1.4). Nothing is received on
  such a call, and FaxRcvdCmd does not run for it.
- faxd/Class1Recv.c++, Class1.h/.c++, Class1Poll.c++: the Class 1 driver sets
  bit 9 when told, keeps the poller's PWD, SEP, CIG and DTC instead of
  treating a DTC as its own DIS echoed back (recvDCSFrames), returns from
  recvBegin on DTC, and turns the line around (pollTransmitBegin: sendBegin,
  the DTC as dis_caps, training forced).
- faxd/FaxModem.h/.c++: the four driver hooks, with defaults that never
  offer or accept polling (Class 2 drivers are unchanged).
- faxd/faxGettyApp.h/.c++: a new config item, PolledCmd, run after every
  polled call with: document (or ""), device, commid, reason (or ""), pages
  sent, caller, CIG, SEP, the holder's job reference, then the call ID values
  as FaxRcvdCmd gets them. Unset by default; Faxbot's engine sets it.

Timing (T.30 5.3.6.1.4, Figure 5-2b): the poller repeats DTC after T4
(3 s +/- 15%) without a response, so the first DCS must start inside it. It
does: the document scan is a few small reads before the DIS, and after the
DTC the send path begins with the 75 ms switching pause and V.21 exactly as
after a DIS. ECM, SSL Fax and the T.38 gateway see an ordinary transmission
from here on.

Known deviation: frames the polled station transmits after the turnaround
(TSI, DCS, PPS, EOP, DCN) keep HylaFAX's X bit = 1 (the station that
received DIS, T.30 5.3.6.1.1), although as the station that sent the DIS it
should set X = 0; only the refusal DCN carries X = 0. HylaFAX+ (getFCF masks
the bit) and spandsp (& 0xFE) ignore the X bit on reception; a poller that
checks it is an integration test item. A caller that sends pages first and
polls in the same call (EOM, then DTC) is not served: the offer is made on
the first DIS of a call only.

